# Stat cards (KPI / summary)

Applies to horizontal **summary stat cards** in `design/` mockups and `frontend/` production UI: icon well on the left (or leading edge) + label and value text on the right.

## In scope

- List page KPI rows (e.g. member user totals, warehouse view counts)
- Form or modal summary strips (e.g. lot/history KPI cards)

## Out of scope

- Table cells, form field rows, page headers, avatars beside long prose — use normal layout rules; do not force stat-card centering there.

## Row alignment (required)

The **card row** flex container must vertically center the icon block against the text column:

| Area | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **Frontend** | Outer card wrapper: `flex items-center` (plus `gap-*`, border, padding as designed) |
| **Design** | Stat card class: `align-items: center` on the row (not `flex-start`) |

The icon **well** (`__icon`, rounded square/circle behind the glyph) still uses internal centering (`items-center justify-center` / flex center on the well) so the Lucide/SVG sits in the middle of the well. This rule is about **row** cross-axis alignment only.

## Reference

- **Frontend:** [`warehouse-view-stat-cards.tsx`](../../frontend/app/[locale]/(admin)/admin/(backoffice)/warehouse/_shared/warehouse-view-stat-cards.tsx)
- **Design CSS:** `.member-user-stat`, `.wh-view-stat`, `.product-list-form__lot-stat` in [`design/css/style.css`](../../design/css/style.css)

When adding a new stat card pattern, match this row alignment in the same change.
